terNACHI, ensuring a high level of professionalism and expertise.","heading":null,"icon":{"url":"https://ggfx-providentestate.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/i/icon_e36dd22ac2.svg"}},{"title":"Cutting Edge Reporting","strapi_id":31,"id":"25d9b762-a3e9-50c0-aca0-eceda0044ede","description":"The use of professional snagging software enables our team to provide detailed, precise documentation of findings.","heading":null,"icon":{"url":"https://ggfx-providentestate.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/i/icon_1_809fc318ec.svg"}},{"title":"Proactive Problem Solving","strapi_id":32,"id":"d88e1b70-2e8b-5b95-9577-809a903caac0","description":"By identifying potential issues early in the handover process, we help our clients avoid  costly repairs and disputes in the future.","heading":null,"icon":{"url":"https://ggfx-providentestate.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/i/icon_2_db0d76442b.svg"}}]},{"id":"d6a8b37c-b039-5451-9976-fa59e783c12f","title":"Discover what our customers are saying about their experiences.","strapi_id":35,"strapi_component":"modules.global-module","heading":"Real reviews from real customers.","choose_module":"reviews_slider","bg_color":"grey","cta_text":null,"design_title":{"data":{"design_title":""}}},{"id":"be2aff72-7111-5a50-9f19-b1031d6ed25a","cta":null,"image":{"url":"https://ggfx-providentestate.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/i/property_snagging_certificate_29ef65a24e.png"},"design_title":{"data":{"design_title":""}},"img_align":"right","strapi_component":"modules.tile-block","strapi_id":734,"title":"We are proudly certified  by InterNACHI","description":{"data":{"description":"<p><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><strong>The premier global association for home inspection excellence, we carry the seal that sets the standard.</strong> When seeking dependable home inspection services, look for the trusted InterNACHI badge – a mark of integrity, expertise, and the highest quality.</span></p>"}},"video_url":null,"heading":null,"icon_stats":[],"bg_color":null,"image_fit":"contain","style":null},{"id":"37565341-d8eb-58e7-99c4-ac057781bd44","title":"Frequently Asked Questions","strapi_id":45,"strapi_component":"modules.faq","cta_text":null,"bg_color":null,"faqs":[{"strapi_id":819,"question":"What is a Snag?","id":"6419e7d6-8f2e-5d06-b8cd-88c6b078dc99","answer":{"data":{"answer":"<p><meta charset=\"utf-8\">A snag is a small defect or a problem found in a property after construction is completed, typically manifesting as incomplete, unfinished, or damaged work. This includes chipped tiles, patched paint jobs, scratched glass, uneven terminations, missing door stoppers, screws, wall cracks, etc. While most snags are cosmetic, MEP (Mechanical, Electrical, and Plumbing) defects can seriously affect daily life, such as improper gas connections, insufficient cooling, moisture inside walls or doors, and incorrect electrical wiring.</p>"}}},{"strapi_id":871,"question":"What is a Snagging Inspection?","id":"5b03b2be-b359-56d8-b45f-8e301e798cf4","answer":{"data":{"answer":"<p>This inspection allows homeowners to identify defects or snags in their property during the Orientation or Visit invitation by the developer, before proceeding with the key handover.</p>"}}},{"strapi_id":872,"question":"Why do I need an Inspection?","id":"e78fab1a-4d95-5933-ac18-7c4990b30e96","answer":{"data":{"answer":"<p>It’s crucial for receiving technical advice on the condition of the property across all aspects (cosmetics, mechanical, electrical, and plumbing) to ensure the property is defect-free before taking the key handover.</p>"}}},{"strapi_id":873,"question":"What is covered in a Snagging Inspection","id":"14ad044e-f09f-5574-82e6-170d7be85a55","answer":{"data":{"answer":"<p>The inspection encompasses every part and item of the property, including cosmetics, MEPs, sanitary ware, appliances, and furniture, as well as specific areas for villas and townhouses like the water pump room, water tank, manholes, garden area, carport, and rooftop.</p>"}}},{"strapi_id":874,"question":"When do I need the Snagging Inspection?","id":"8f1e3e8b-cb61-5d14-a8bd-59842c39c91a","answer":{"data":{"answer":"<p>The ideal timing for a snagging inspection is at the Orientation of the property before completing the handover process with the developer.&nbsp;</p>"}}},{"strapi_id":875,"question":"Why do I need 3rd party Snagging Professionals?","id":"9f4e927c-9b12-50c6-bc13-9b2132c5165c","answer":{"data":{"answer":"<p>Third-party professionals bring technical knowledge and experience, employing tools and equipment to uncover hidden defects, offering an expert opinion on the property’s condition.</p>"}}},{"strapi_id":876,"question":"Who is responsible for rectifying the Snags?","id":"50068dfb-d124-5d81-b393-c4941d3c91d8","answer":{"data":{"answer":"<p>The developer bears the responsibility for rectifying all identified snags and defects, allowing for a De-snag inspection before the key handover.</p>"}}},{"strapi_id":877,"question":"How long do developers take to rectify all the Snags? ","id":"cbf0a684-6c8c-5480-9491-07049df73c4c","answer":{"data":{"answer":"<p>While timelines can vary depending on the property size and number of snags, the average rectification period is about 20 to 30 days.</p>"}}}]},{"id":"cb248513-87a5-5c21-b3ee-8b3b67671a86","title":"Searching for an expert property service?","content":{"data":{"content":"<p><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\">Contact Our Experts</span></p>"}},"stats":[],"form":"Snagging","strapi_component":"modules.form-module","strapi_id":13,"show_contact":false,"cta":null,"icon_stats":[{"text":"Professional Expertise","strapi_id":1193,"image":{"url":"https://ggfx-providentestate.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/i/check_cricle_f92cf7c837.svg"},"id":"151c4ca5-327c-5a50-a9ac-826dfabc12b0"},{"text":"Cutting Edge Reporting","strapi_id":1194,"image":{"url":"https://ggfx-providentestate.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/i/check_cricle_f92cf7c837.svg"},"id":"dacf6331-3834-585e-99af-bd365612